{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs",
  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/NodeContents]/fn[node_content]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This storage-only consumer must delegate load/store using node_path\n without resolving contents. NodeContents requires the callback, but invoking\n this guard would violate the no-content-read invariant of the test.\n Other graph fixtures exercise content resolution."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs#impl[StoredGraph/NodeContents]/fn[node_content]` is appropriate.\n\n- **Form:** The citation is a fenced `{cite}` on an explicit function with a body. That is a permitted form, and the commentary is fenced.\n- **Substance:** The commentary gives a real reason for the missing coverage. `NodeContents` requires the callback, so the storage-only fixture must define it. The fixture's invariant is that storage operations delegate through `node_path` and never resolve contents, so the body is a `panic!` guard that should never run. This is not an appeal to difficulty.\n- **Agreement with the source:**\n  - `StoredGraph`'s `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` only call `self.0.load` and `self.0.store` with `self.node_path(node)`. They never resolve contents.\n  - `StoredReview::execute` does not read contents either.\n  - The only library callers of `node_content` are `InspectionContext::prepare_read` and `dependencies_are_current` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs`. These are reached only for content dependencies, and the records in this test have none.\n  - The claim that other fixtures exercise content resolution is true. `Memory/NodeContents/node_content` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` and in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs` are real implementations.\n- **Redundancy:** The item has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to `habeas:coverage`, so the citation is not redundant.\n\nI found no gap.",
